g air, rather than drain water, to flow back if a clog occurs.<\/p>\n<br>\n<h4>Do I need an Air Gap faucet?<\/h4>\n<p>The need for an Air Gap faucet depends on local building codes, not the RO system itself. Some areas require Air Gap faucets for RO systems, so it's important to check local regulations before installation.<\/p>\n<br>\n<h4>What does a Metpure Air Gap faucet include?<\/h4>\n<p>Metpure Air Gap faucets come with a vent hole, two ports for drain IN and OUT, and pre-attached tubing, making installation easy and ensuring backflow prevention.<\/p>","width":"50%","block_custom_class":"","animations":"inherit"}},"template--15947484627135__db438752-413c-4d7d-91e5-255e47ac52fa-16784777673fc0ad21-0":{"type":"text","disabled":true,"settings":{"title":"","subheading":"","text":"<h4><strong>What is an Air Gap faucet?<\/strong><\/h4><h4><br\/>An Air Gap faucet dispenses water like standard faucets but includes a built-in vent to prevent backflow. This design protects reverse osmosis (RO) systems from contamination by allowing air, rather than drain water, to flow back if a clog occurs.<br\/><br\/><br\/>Do I need an Air Gap faucet?<br\/><br\/>The need for an Air Gap faucet depends on local building codes, not the RO system itself. Some areas require Air Gap faucets for RO systems, so it's important to check local regulations before installation.<\/h4><h4><strong>What does a Metpure Air Gap faucet include?<br\/><\/strong><br\/>Metpure Air Gap faucets come with a vent hole, two ports for drain IN and OUT, and pre-attached tubing, making installation easy and ensuring backflow prevention.<\/h4>","width":"50%","alignment":"center","align_text":"left","text_size":"medium","text_color":"black","button_label":"","button_link":"","button_style":"sf__btn-primary","button_size":"","block_custom_class":"","animations":"inherit"}},"f7c43b97-9242-4c0b-b437-ad4e96b9e1da":{"type":"image","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/airgap.webp","link":"shopify:\/\/collections\/air